---
import { PUBLIC_CONTACT_FORM } from 'astro:env/client';

import ObfuscatedText from '@/components/ObfuscatedText.astro';
import ProtectedEmail from '@/components/ProtectedEmail.astro';
import { address } from '@/lib/legal-address';
import { siteConfig } from '@/lib/site';

// English translation of PrivacyPolicyDe.astro. Keep both in step: same sections in the same
// order, and the contact form section exists exactly when the form is built in. The German text
// is the legally binding original.
let section = 0;
const next = () => (section += 1);
---

<section lang="en" id="en" aria-labelledby="privacy-en">
  <h2 id="privacy-en">Privacy policy</h2>
  <p class="notice-inline">
    This is a translation to make the text easier to understand. The German version below is the
    legally binding original.
  </p>

  <h3>{next()}. Controller</h3>
  <p>The controller for data processing on this website within the meaning of the GDPR is:</p>
  <address>
    {siteConfig.name}
    <br />
    <ObfuscatedText text={address.street} />
    <br />
    <ObfuscatedText text={`${address.zip} ${address.city}`} />
    <br />
    Email: <ProtectedEmail address={siteConfig.email} />
  </address>

  <h3>{next()}. Hosting and server log files</h3>
  <p>
    This website is hosted by Cloudflare, Inc. (101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA) and
    delivered through its global network. When you visit the website, Cloudflare processes
    technically necessary connection data. This includes in particular:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>IP address</li>
    <li>date and time of the request</li>
    <li>the page requested (URL) and the page visited before (referrer)</li>
    <li>browser type, operating system and other details of your device (user agent)</li>
    <li>security-related information to detect and defend against attacks and bots</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The processing serves to provide the website securely and reliably and to defend against abuse.
    The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in secure and efficient operation).
    Cloudflare may transfer data to the USA. Cloudflare is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy
    Framework, and the EU Commission's standard contractual clauses are in place as well. A data
    processing agreement exists with Cloudflare.
  </p>
  <p>
    As part of its bot protection, Cloudflare may set technically necessary cookies (for example
    <code>__cf_bm</code>). They serve security purposes only and do not require consent. The website
    itself sets no cookies of its own.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare stores this data only as long as necessary for the purposes stated. I do not analyse
    it myself and I do not keep visitor statistics.
  </p>

  {PUBLIC_CONTACT_FORM && (
    <>
      <h3>{next()}. Contact form</h3>
      <p>
        You can write to me through a contact form on the home page. The form only works with
        JavaScript enabled. Alternatively you can always reach me by email (see the section
        &ldquo;Contact by email&rdquo;).
      </p>

      <h4>Which data is processed</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your entries in the form: name, email address and the text of your message. Please do not
          enter sensitive data (for example health data) that I do not need to reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          When you submit the form, your IP address and the time, as with every visit to the
          website, by Cloudflare (see the section &ldquo;Hosting and server log files&rdquo;).
        </li>
        <li>
          A counter to protect against spam and abuse: a non-reversible hash value is created from
          your IP address using a secret key. It is stored together with the number of your messages
          at Cloudflare (Workers KV) for two hours at most and then deleted automatically. The IP
          address itself is not stored there.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Technical safeguards without storing anything on your device</h4>
      <p>
        As soon as you click into the form, your browser fetches a signed time stamp. It shows that
        a person took time to write, and it is kept only in your browser&apos;s memory. There is
        also a hidden field that only bots fill in. Neither contains any information about you, sets
        cookies or stores anything on your device.
      </p>

      <h4>Purpose and legal basis</h4>
      <p>
        I process your data solely to handle and answer your enquiry. The legal basis is Art.
        6(1)(b) GDPR where your enquiry concerns pre-contractual measures or a contract (for example
        an enquiry about a position or a project), and otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate
        interest in answering enquiries). The counter for abuse protection is based on Art. 6(1)(f)
        GDPR (legitimate interest in trouble-free operation and protection against spam). Consent is
        not required and is not requested.
      </p>

      <h4>Path of your message and recipients</h4>
      <p>
        Your message is received and checked by a function at Cloudflare (Cloudflare Pages
        Functions) and handed over through an encrypted connection (STARTTLS) to the mail server of
        IONOS SE (Elgendorfer Str. 57, 56410 Montabaur, Germany), where my mailbox is hosted. I
        receive it from there like any other email; your email address serves as the reply address.
        I do not store the content of your message in a database and I do not write it to logs. No
        further service provider (for example no form or newsletter service) is involved. Data
        processing agreements exist with Cloudflare and IONOS. For the transfer to the USA see the
        section &ldquo;Hosting and server log files&rdquo;.
      </p>

      <h4>Storage period</h4>
      <p>
        Your message and your details stay in my mailbox as long as necessary to handle your
        enquiry. After that I delete them, unless statutory retention obligations apply (for example
        under Section 257 HGB and Section 147 AO for business correspondence). The hash value from
        the spam protection is deleted automatically after two hours at the latest.
      </p>

      <h4>Obligation to provide data</h4>
      <p>
        Providing your name, email address and message is voluntary. Without them I cannot answer
        your enquiry through the form. You can always write to me directly by email instead.
      </p>
    </>
  )}

  <h3>{next()}. Contact by email</h3>
  <p>
    If you send me an email, I process your details (email address, content of the message) solely
    to handle your enquiry. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (pre-contractual measures) or Art.
    6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in answering enquiries). The mailbox is operated by IONOS SE
    (Elgendorfer Str. 57, 56410 Montabaur, Germany), with which a data processing agreement exists.
    Your data is deleted as soon as the enquiry is settled and no statutory retention obligations
    apply (see above, for example Section 257 HGB and Section 147 AO for business correspondence).
    Please note that an unencrypted email can in principle be read by third parties in transit.
  </p>

  <h3>{next()}. Cookies and storage on your device</h3>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies of its own and stores no information on your device (for example in
    local storage), and it does not read any such information. Consent under Section 25 TDDDG is
    therefore not required. For Cloudflare&apos;s technically necessary security cookies see the
    section &ldquo;Hosting and server log files&rdquo;.
  </p>

  <h3>{next()}. No analytics or tracking services, no external content</h3>
  <p>
    This website uses no analytics, tracking or advertising services and embeds no external content
    such as maps, videos or social media widgets. Fonts are delivered locally by this website, no
    connection to third-party font servers is made.
  </p>

  <h3>{next()}. External links</h3>
  <p>
    This website contains links to external sites (for example GitHub, LinkedIn). Merely visiting
    this website does not transfer any data to them. The privacy notices of the respective provider
    apply only once you click a link.
  </p>

  <h3>{next()}. SSL / TLS encryption</h3>
  <p>
    For security reasons this website uses SSL / TLS encryption. You can recognise an encrypted
    connection by the address bar of your browser (&ldquo;https://&rdquo;) and the lock symbol.
  </p>

  <h3>{next()}. No automated decision-making</h3>
  <p>
    There is no automated decision-making, including profiling, within the meaning of Art. 22 GDPR.
  </p>

  <h3>{next()}. Your rights</h3>
  <p>Within the scope of the applicable statutory provisions you have the right at any time to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access to your stored personal data (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
    <li>rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
    <li>erasure of your data (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
    <li>restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
    <li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
    <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
    <li>
      withdraw consent you have given, with effect for the future (Art. 7(3) GDPR). At present no
      processing on this website is based on consent.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Right to object:</strong> Where I process data on the basis of legitimate interests
    (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR), you can object to this at any time on grounds relating to your particular
    situation. I will then no longer process the data unless I can demonstrate compelling legitimate
    grounds.
  </p>
  <p>
    An informal email to the address above is enough to exercise your rights. You also have the
    right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, in particular in the
    member state of your habitual residence, place of work or the place of the alleged infringement.
    The authority responsible for me is the data protection supervisory authority of the German
    state in which I live.
  </p>

  <h3>{next()}. Last updated</h3>
  <p>
    Status: October 2026. I will update this policy when the website or the legal requirements
    change.
  </p>
</section>
